From 8a1a6372eead2a7f4df42f9c5d97466337cd7a27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Round 7: Serialize SIR metrics from typed structs

Build SIR metrics from Serialize structs whose fields follow the sorted
key order of a serde_json::Value map, including sorted mirrors that
borrow the traced FspResult and its snapshots, and serialize them
straight to the raw metrics JSON. No Value tree is built and the trace is
no longer converted with to_value first. A unit test compares the typed
bytes with the previous json! construction, traced and untraced, with
and without holdout points.

Workload: trace (12 traced SIR candidates, full records), 11 samples.
Before median: 1.090 ms. After median: 0.817 ms. Speedup: 1.33x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
